# Git and Monorepo

## Commit messages

Commits follow the conventional-commit + git-cz emoji style already in the history:

- `feat: 🎸 <subject>` — new feature
- `fix: 🐛 <subject>` — bug fix
- `fix: 💄 <subject>` — visual/style fix
- `chore: <subject>` — tooling, deps, housekeeping
- `refactor: <subject>` — behavior-preserving restructuring
- `docs: ✏️ <subject>` — documentation

Subject is imperative and lowercase ("add invitation flow", not "Added invitation flow."). Match this format exactly when authoring commits.

## Monorepo

pnpm workspaces + Nx.

- Internal packages are `@hype-stack/*` and referenced with `"workspace:*"` — never a version number.
- Shared code used by multiple apps lives in `packages/`; code used by one app stays inside that app. Don't promote to `packages/` until a second real consumer exists.
- Run app-scoped scripts with `pnpm --filter @hype-stack/<app> <script>`; repo-wide targets run through the root scripts (Nx handles caching and ordering).
- Add dependencies to the specific app or package that uses them, not the workspace root (root is for tooling only).
- After changing generated types or cross-app contracts (backend routes, socket events, enums), regenerate with `pnpm generate` so dependent apps pick up the new types.
